## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical streaming state management, windowing, and late data handling in KCNA.

## Key Concepts
- Windowed aggregation by userId using 10-minute tumbling windows
- Watermark and 2-minute lateness tolerance for out-of-order events
- Per-window state management with eviction policies
- At-least-once guarantees via offset committing after emission
- Canary coverage with mixed event timings

## Code Example
```javascript
const WINDOW_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;
const LATE_MS = 2 * 60 * 1000;

function onMessage(msg, commitFn) {
  const { userId, ts, score } = JSON.parse(msg.value);
  const windowStart = Math.floor(ts / WINDOW_MS) * WINDOW_MS;
  const windowEnd = windowStart + WINDOW_MS;
  const stateKey = `${userId}:${windowStart}`;

  if (ts < watermark - LATE_MS) return; // drop late

  state[stateKey] = (state[stateKey] || 0) + score;
  watermark = Math.max(watermark, ts);

  if (watermark >= windowEnd + LATE_MS && !emitted.has(stateKey)) {
    emit('activity_agg', { userId, windowStart, windowEnd, sum: state[stateKey] });
    emitted.add(stateKey);
    delete state[stateKey];
  }

  commitFn();
}

function onPartitionsAssigned(partitions) {
  state = restoreState(partitions);
  watermark = restoreWatermark();
}

function onPartitionsRevoked() {
  checkpointState(state, watermark);
  state = {};
}

function commitOffsets(offsets) {
  consumer.commit(offsets);
}
```

## Canary Test
Send events with userId='u1' at t=0s (score=10), t=300s (score=20), then late at t=540s (score=30, within 2-min tolerance). Verify sum=60 emitted for window [0s, 600s).

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests per-key stateful processing, TTL-based windowing, and idempotence across replays—core KCNA concepts—while exercising cross-event aggregation and emission semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key in-memory or stateful session store with a 30-second TTL
- Idempotent emits using a deterministic sessionId (userId:start)
- Out-of-order arrivals handled via lastEventTs and session boundaries
- At-least-once delivery guaranteed by committing offsets only after emit

## Code Example
```javascript
function onMessage(ctx, msg) {
  const session = sessionStore().getOrCreate(msg.userId, () => ({
    startTs: msg.timestamp,
    endTs: msg.timestamp,
    count: 0,
    lastEventTs: msg.timestamp
  }));
  session.endTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.lastEventTs = msg.timestamp;
  session.count++;
  sessionStore().setTtl(msg.userId, 30000, () => {
    ctx.emit('sessions', {
      userId: msg.userId,
      sessionStart: session.startTs,
      sessionEnd: session.endTs,
      eventCount: session.count
    });
    sessionStore().remove(msg.userId);
  });
}

function commitOffsets() {
  ctx.commit();
}

function sessionStore() {
  return ctx.state();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced fairness and isolation in a multi-tenant KCNA cluster; demonstrates practical reliability under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket, leaky bucket)
- Global throughput vs. per-tenant isolation
- Distributed state store for buckets (Redis, etc.)
- Backpressure mechanisms and producer signaling
- Canary strategy and measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allow(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}

// Global limiter wrapping per-tenant buckets
class TenantRateController {
  constructor(tenants, globalRate) {
    this.buckets = new Map();
    this.globalLimiter = new TokenBucket(globalRate, globalRate * 2);
    for (const [id, quota] of tenants) {
      this.buckets.set(id, new TokenBucket(quota.rate, quota.burst));
    }
  }

  tryProcess(tenantId, n = 1) {
    const bucket = this.buckets.get(tenantId);
    if (!bucket || !bucket.allow(n)) return false;
    if (!this.globalLimiter.allow(n)) {
      bucket.tokens += n; // rollback tenant token
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

